Database Migration Walkthrough
This walkthrough explains how to use the newly set up Alembic integration to manage database schema changes automatically.

Prerequisites
Ensure you have the dependencies installed:

pip install -r requirements.txt
How to Make Schema Changes
Modify Models: Update your SQLAlchemy models in 
app/models.py
. For example, add a new column to a table.
Generate Migration: Run the following command to auto-generate a migration script based on your changes:
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "Describe your change here"
This will create a new file in alembic/versions/.
Apply Migration: Apply the changes to the database:
alembic upgrade head
Verification
You can verify the current state of the database by checking the alembic_version table, which tracks the latest applied migration hash.

Rollback
To undo the last migration:

alembic downgrade -1
Setup details
Configuration: alembic.ini and alembic/ directory have been created.
Environment: 
alembic/env.py
 is configured to load environment variables from 
.env
 and import your models from app.models.
Database: The database is located at 
backend/db/payment.db
 (as configured in 
.env
).